  ('b21f9628-15ed-4469-8d80-b67772633a44', 'd37c1e13-9c86-4b42-8657-16a4c0df1eb1', 'db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7', 'executeTask', 'Create a simple invoice for TechCorp consulting services', '{}'::jsonb, '{"success":true,"response":"I''ll help you create a consulting invoice for TechCorp. Here''s the invoice structure:\n\n**Invoice Details:**\n- **Invoice Number**: INV-10238 (next in sequence)\n- **Client**: TechCorp\n- **Invoice Date**: January 26, 2025\n- **Due Date**: February 10, 2025 (Net 15 - their preferred terms)\n\n**Services:**\n- Strategic Technology Consulting: 10 hours × $175/hour\n- Implementation Planning: 5 hours × $175/hour\n- Documentation & Training: $500 (fixed fee)\n\n**Payment Information:**\n- **Subtotal**: $2,750\n- **Tax (if applicable)**: $0\n- **Total Amount Due**: $2,750\n\n**Payment Terms:**\n- **Payment Terms**: Net 15 days\n- **Payment Methods**: ACH (preferred), Check, Wire Transfer\n- **Late Fee**: 1.5% per month on overdue balances\n\nPlease review the details, and if everything looks correct, we can finalize the invoice for TechCorp. Let me know if you need any adjustments or additional information.","metadata":{"agentName":"Invoice Agent","agentType":"specialist","contextUsed":true,"contextLength":8450,"processedAt":"2025-07-29T16:02:59.361Z"}}', '{"agentName":"Invoice Agent","agentType":"specialist","contextUsed":true,"processedAt":"2025-07-29T16:02:59.361Z","contextLength":8450}'::jsonb, 'completed', 100, 'Task created, waiting for execution...', '{}'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-29T16:02:59.362+00:00', 300, '{}'::jsonb, '2025-07-29T16:02:56.481839+00:00', '2025-07-29T16:02:59.51098+00:00', 'text', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('43b38ad5-b883-4221-b3ab-ea93e1b549fc', '52d6b373-7f83-4eac-b9ff-e42b7f168f29', 'db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7', 'executeTask', 'Write a requirements document for a weather control system', '{}'::jsonb, '{"response":"# Technical Requirements Document (TRD) for Weather Control System\n\n## 1. System Overview\nThe Weather Control System is a complex software application designed to monitor, predict, and control weather patterns. It consists of various components including Weather Monitoring, Weather Prediction, Climate Control, Data Collection System, Machine Learning Algorithms, Control Interface, User Dashboard, Settings Configuration, Alert Notifications, Weather APIs, Sensor Networks, Access Control, and Data Encryption. The system leverages advanced technologies to provide accurate weather data, predictions, and control capabilities.\n\n## 2. Technical Architecture\nThe system''s technical architecture includes the following components:\n- **Weather Monitoring**: Collects real-time weather data from various sensors and sources.\n- **Weather Prediction**: Utilizes machine learning algorithms to forecast weather patterns.\n- **Climate Control**: Controls environmental conditions based on weather predictions.\n- **Data Collection System**: Stores and manages historical weather data for analysis.\n- **Machine Learning Algorithms**: Analyzes data to improve weather prediction accuracy.\n- **Control Interface**: Allows users to interact with the system to monitor and control weather conditions.\n- **User Dashboard**: Provides a graphical interface for users to view weather information and system status.\n- **Settings Configuration**: Enables users to customize system settings and preferences.\n- **Alert Notifications**: Notifies users about severe weather conditions or system anomalies.\n- **Weather APIs**: Interfaces with external weather services to enhance data accuracy.\n- **Sensor Networks**: Deployed sensors for data collection and monitoring.\n- **Access Control**: Manages user authentication and authorization within the system.\n- **Data Encryption**: Secures sensitive weather data to ensure confidentiality.\n\nInteractions between these components are well defined to ensure smooth operation and data flow.\n\n## 3. Database Requirements\nThe system requires a robust database to store weather data, user settings, and system configurations. The database should support high write and read throughput, as well as the ability to scale to handle large volumes of data. Data models should be optimized for efficient retrieval and analysis, while storage should be reliable and fault-tolerant to prevent data loss.\n\n## 4. API Specifications\nThe system should expose APIs for integrating with external services, accessing weather data, and controlling climate settings. APIs should follow industry-standard protocols such as REST or GraphQL and use common data formats like JSON or XML for seamless communication with other systems.\n\n## 5. Security Requirements\nSecurity is paramount in the Weather Control System. The system must implement strong authentication mechanisms to verify user identities and authorize access to sensitive features. Data encryption should be employed to protect data both at rest and in transit. Compliance with industry regulations such as GDPR should be ensured to safeguard user privacy.\n\n## 6. Performance Requirements\nThe system should be designed for high performance, scalability, and responsiveness. It should be able to handle a large number of concurrent users, process real-time data streams, and deliver timely weather predictions. Load balancing, caching, and optimization techniques should be utilized to enhance performance.\n\n## 7. Infrastructure Requirements\nDeployment of the system requires a robust infrastructure capable of hosting the various components securely. Monitoring tools should be in place to track system health and performance. Backup and disaster recovery mechanisms should be implemented to ensure data integrity and availability in case of failures.\n\n## 8. Integration Requirements\nThe Weather Control System may need to integrate with external weather services, sensor networks, and third-party systems to enhance its capabilities. Data flows between these systems should be seamless and well-defined to ensure accurate data exchange and interoperability.\n\n## 9. Development Standards\nDevelopment of the system should adhere to coding best practices, testing requirements, and comprehensive documentation. Code reviews, unit testing, integration testing, and continuous integration practices should be followed to maintain code quality and ensure system reliability.\n\n## 10. Deployment Strategy\nA robust deployment strategy should be implemented using Continuous Integration/Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) pipelines to automate the deployment process. Multiple environments for development, testing, staging, and production should be set up to facilitate controlled releases. Rollback procedures should be in place to revert to previous versions in case of deployment failures.\n\nThis TRD provides a detailed technical blueprint for the implementation of the Weather Control System, emphasizing high performance, security, scalability, and reliability. It serves as a guide for architects, senior developers, and DevOps engineers involved in building and maintaining the system.","analysis":{"intent":"Create a requirements document for a weather control system","scope":"large","clarity":"medium","urgency":"normal","domain":"technical","confidence":0.8,"key_indicators":["requirements document","weather control system"],"missing_info":["specific functionalities needed","target users","integration requirements"],"summary":"The user is requesting the creation of a detailed requirements document for a weather control system. The scope is large and involves technical aspects. While the request is fairly clear, more information is needed on specific functionalities, target users, and integration requirements."},"metadata":{"document_type":"trd","complexity":"high","features":["Weather Monitoring","Weather Prediction","Climate Control","Data Collection System","Machine Learning Algorithms","Control Interface","User Dashboard","Settings Configuration","Alert Notifications","Weather APIs","Sensor Networks","Access Control","Data Encryption"],"workflow_step":"completed","generated_at":"2025-07-29T18:04:32.614077","processing_type":"modular-langgraph-workflow","processing_method":"real_llm_calls","agent_type":"requirements_writer","tools_used":["langgraph","real-llm-calls","modular-nodes","state-management"],"workflow_steps_completed":["analyze_request","determine_document_type","extract_features","assess_complexity","generate_document","finalize_response"],"method":"processTask","originalParams":{"method":"executeTask","prompt":"Write a requirements document for a weather control system","taskId":"43b38ad5-b883-4221-b3ab-ea93e1b549fc","currentUser":{"id":"db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7","email":"testuser@golfergeek.com","aud":"authenticated","role":"authenticated","appMetadata":{"provider":"email","providers":["email"]},"userMetadata":{"email_verified":true},"phone":"","emailConfirmedAt":"2025-05-22T14:46:52.570Z","confirmedAt":"2025-05-22T14:46:52.570Z","lastSignInAt":"2025-07-29T23:02:36.129Z","createdAt":"2025-05-22T14:46:52.557Z","updatedAt":"2025-07-29T23:02:36.132Z","identities":[{"identity_id":"bd517515-cb47-40de-ae10-5ac590c1c29e","id":"db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7","user_id":"db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7","identity_data":{"email":"testuser@golfergeek.com","email_verified":false,"phone_verified":false,"sub":"db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7"},"provider":"email","last_sign_in_at":"2025-05-22T14:46:52.566752Z","created_at":"2025-05-22T14:46:52.566827Z","updated_at":"2025-05-22T14:46:52.566827Z","email":"testuser@golfergeek.com"}]},"authToken":"eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IkxwM1hCMXIvL0ZEQzNUSjM