  ('6aac2f6c-b9f7-4f7f-9945-19f1a45bab59', '098389a4-5325-4411-a61f-477d2f93d480', 'db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7', 'executeTask', 'Hello, can you help me with onboarding information?', '{}'::jsonb, '{"success":true,"response":"Of course, I''d be happy to assist you with onboarding information! Onboarding is the process through which new employees receive the necessary information, tools, and resources to become acclimated to the company and their new role.\n\nThe onboarding policy exists to ensure that new employees have a smooth transition into the organization, understand their roles and responsibilities, and feel welcomed and supported. This process helps to set clear expectations, align new employees with the company culture, and provide them with the necessary training to succeed in their positions.\n\nHere are some specific steps you should follow during the onboarding process:\n1. Complete all required paperwork and documentation as provided by the HR department.\n2. Participate in orientation sessions to learn about company policies, benefits, and procedures.\n3. Meet with your manager to discuss job expectations, goals, and performance metrics.\n4. Engage in any training programs or on-the-job learning activities as required for your role.\n\nDuring the onboarding process, you can expect to receive information about the company''s mission, values, and culture, as well as details about your benefits package, work schedule, and any relevant training or development opportunities.\n\nIf you have any questions or need additional support during the onboarding process, please don''t hesitate to reach out to your HR representative or directly contact me, and I''ll be more than happy to assist you every step of the way. Welcome aboard!","metadata":{"agentType":"specialist","functionStatus":"executed","processedAt":"2025-08-06T01:33:01.926Z","method":"processTask","originalParams":{"method":"executeTask","prompt":"Hello, can you help me with onboarding inform