  ('c82583d9-41b4-4f85-a133-19f090ed843c', 'a5600c89-50f5-45b1-9569-13c9ec1512e3', 'db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7', 'handle_request', 'Write a blog post about AI in healthcare', '{"userMessage":"Write a blog post about AI in healthcare"}'::jsonb, NULL, '{}'::jsonb, 'failed', 0, 'Task created, waiting for execution...', '{}'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, NULL, 'Hiverarchy authentication failed: No access token received from Hiverarchy', NULL, NULL, NULL, 300, '{}'::jsonb, '2025-07-30T15:03:34.631022+00:00', '2025-07-30T15:03:35.17301+00:00', 'text', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('796975b6-435b-4a51-a372-afcd981c1f6f', '47ee8d3d-f85b-4a2f-ace2-ffdb12081018', '09f41d4d-1697-4141-a0de-3e258faae92b', 'process', 'You write me a blog post about playing golf in the rain.', '{}'::jsonb, '{"success":true,"response":"# 📋 Marketing Content Package\n\n**MARKETING CONTENT PACKAGE**\n\n**Blog Post: Mastering the Elements: A Guide to Playing Golf in the Rain**\n\n**Introduction:**\nEmbrace the challenge of playing golf in the rain with our comprehensive guide. Discover how to enhance your skills, adapt your strategy, and enjoy a unique golfing experience despite the weather.\n\n**Tips for Playing in the Rain:**\n1. **Proper Gear:** Invest in quality rain gear to stay dry and focused.\n2. **Club Selection:** Adjust clubs for wet conditions to improve ball control.\n3. **Grip and Stance:** Modify grip and stance for stability on slippery surfaces.\n4. **Mindset:** Approach rainy rounds with a positive mindset to boost performance.\n5. **Ball Position:** Tee the ball higher to prevent waterlogging and maintain distance.\n\n**Benefits of Playing Golf in the Rain:**\n- **Improved Adaptability:** Enhance resilience and adaptability on the course.\n- **Skill Development:** Improve ball-striking and shot-making skills.\n- **Enjoyment:** Experience a unique and rewarding golfing adventure.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nDon''t let a little rain stop you from enjoying the game you love. Embrace the challenge, elevate your skills, and show the elements who''s boss on the course!\n\n**Call to Action:**\nShare your rain-soaked golfing adventures with us and inspire others to embrace the elements. Remember, a little rain shouldn''t dampen your passion for golf!\n\n**Implementation Guidance:**\n- Incorporate relevant keywords like ''playing golf in the rain'' and ''rainy day golf tips'' throughout the blog post for SEO optimization.\n- Maintain a consistent brand voice and tone to strengthen brand identity and engage the audience emotionally.\n\n---\n\n**Social Media Post: Mastering the Elements: A Golfer''s Guide to Playing in the Rain**\n\n**Introduction:**\nDiscover the thrill of playing golf in the rain and why it can be a rewarding and exhilarating experience for true golf enthusiasts.\n\n**Tips for Playing Golf in the Rain:**\n1. **Stay Dry:** Invest in quality waterproof gear to stay comfortable and focused.\n2. **Adjust Your Strategy:** Make strategic adjustments to your game for wet conditions.\n3. **Stay Positive:** Embrace the challenge and appreciate the beauty of a rain-soaked course.\n\n**Share Your Rainy Golf Experience:**\nJoin the #RainyGolfChallenge and share your stories, tips, and photos to inspire fellow golf enthusiasts to embrace the rain on the course.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nImmerse yourself in the elements, challenge your skills, and deepen your connection with the game by playing golf in the rain. Tee off with confidence, rain or shine!\n\n**Implementation Guidance:**\n- Use hashtags like #RainyGolfChallenge to encourage user-generated content and engagement.\n- Share the post across social media platforms to reach a wider audience and inspire more players to embrace the elements.\n\n---\n\n**Actionable Recommendations:**\n1. Implement meta descriptions for the blog post to improve search visibility and click-through rates.\n2. Infuse emotional storytelling in social media posts to deepen audience engagement and connection with the content.\n3. Share the blog post on social media platforms with a consistent brand voice and tone to strengthen brand identity.\n\n**Next Steps:**\n- Publish the blog post on your website and optimize it for SEO with relevant keywords.\n- Share the social media post across platforms and encourage user participation in the #RainyGolfChallenge.\n- Monitor engagement metrics and user responses to refine future marketing strategies.\n\nThis comprehensive Marketing Content Package combines compelling storytelling, actionable tips, and engagement strategies to inspire golf enthusiasts to embrace the challenge of playing golf in the rain.\n\n## Individual Content Pieces\n\n### Blog Post Writer\nTitle: Mastering the Elements: A Guide to Playing Golf in the Rain\n\nIntroduction:\nAs golf enthusiasts, we all know the thrill of hitting the perfect shot on a sunny day. But what about those rainy days when the course is wet, and the skies are cloudy? Don''t let a little rain dampen your love for the game! In this comprehensive guide, we will explore the art of playing golf in the rain and how you can still enjoy a great round despite the weather.\n\nEmbracing the Challenge:\nPlaying golf in the rain presents a unique set of challenges that can actually enhance your skills and test your adaptability. The rain alters the course conditions, requiring you to adjust your strategy and approach. By mastering the elements, you can improve your game and gain a competitive edge over fair-weather golfers.\n\nTips for Playing in the Rain:\n1. Proper Gear: Invest in quality rain gear, including waterproof jackets, pants, and gloves. Stay dry to maintain your comfort and focus throughout the round.\n2. Club Selection: Adjust your club selection based on the wet conditions. Opt for more lofted clubs to help you get the ball in the air and avoid skidding on the wet grass.\n3. Grip and Stance: Modify your grip and stance to account for the slippery conditions. Use a lighter grip pressure and widen your stance for better stability and control.\n4. Mindset: Embrace the challenge of playing in the rain with a positive mindset. Stay focused, adapt to the conditions, and see it as an opportunity to improve your skills.\n5. Ball Position: Tee the ball slightly higher to prevent it from getting waterlogged and losing distance. Adjust your ball position based on the lie and conditions of the fairway.\n\nBenefits of Playing Golf in the Rain:\n- Improved Adaptability: Playing in adverse weather conditions enhances your adaptability and resilience on the course.\n- Skill Development: Mastering the art of playing in the rain can improve your ball-striking, shot-making, and overall performance.\n- Enjoyment: Embracing the challenge of playing in the rain can lead to a unique and enjoyable golfing experience that you wouldn''t get on a sunny day.\n\nConclusion:\nPlaying golf in the rain may not be everyone''s cup of tea, but for those willing to embrace the challenge, it can be a rewarding and enriching experience. By following the tips outlined in this guide and approaching the game with a positive mindset, you can elevate your skills, test your adaptability, and enjoy the beauty of golf in all weather conditions. So, next time the rain clouds gather, grab your gear, hit the course, and show the elements who''s boss!\n\nCall to Action:\nReady to take on the challenge of playing golf in the rain? Share your rain-soaked golfing adventures with us in the comments below and inspire others to embrace the elements on the course! Remember, a little rain shouldn''t stop you from enjoying the game you love.\n\n### Social Media Specialist\nTitle: Mastering the Elements: A Golfer''s Guide to Playing in the Rain\n\nIntroduction:\nFor avid golfers, there''s nothing quite like the thrill of teeing off under ominous rain clouds, the smell of petrichor in the air, and the challenge of navigating a wet course. While many might seek shelter when the rain starts falling, true golf enthusiasts know that playing in the rain can be a rewarding and exhilarating experience.\n\nWhy Play Golf in the Rain?\n1. Sharpen Your Skills: Playing in adverse weather conditions can help improve your game by forcing you to adapt your strategy, focus on precision, and test your mental toughness.\n2. Enjoy Quieter Courses: Rainy days often mean fewer golfers on the course, giving you the opportunity for a more peaceful and serene round.\n3. Embrace the Elements: Golf is an outdoor sport, and playing in the rain allows you to connect with nature and experience the game in a different light.\n\nTips for Playing Golf in the Rain:\n1. Stay Dry: Invest in quality waterproof gear, including a reliable rain suit, waterproof golf shoes, and an umbrella to keep yourself comfortable and focused.\n2. Adjust Your Strategy: Wet conditions require adjustments to your game, such as club selection, ball placement, and swing technique. Take your time to assess the course and make strategic decisions.\n3. Stay Positive: A positive attitude is key to enjoying a rainy round of golf. Embrace the challenge, focus on the present moment, and appreciate the beauty of the rain-soaked course.\n\nShare Your Rainy Golf Experience:\nHave you ever braved the rain for a round of golf? Share your stories, tips, and photos with us using the hashtag #RainyGolfChallenge. Let''s celebrate the spirit of golfing in all weather conditions and inspire fellow golf enthusiasts to embrace the rain!\n\nConclusion:\nPlaying golf in the rain is not just about hitting the ball; it''s about immersing yourself in the elements, challenging your skills, and fostering a deeper connection with the game. So next time the rain clouds roll in, don''t shy away from the course—embrace the challenge, gear up, and tee off with confidence. Remember, a little rain can''t dampen the passion of a true golfer!\n\nShare this post with your fellow golf enthusiasts and let''s spread the love for golfing in all weather conditions. Together, we can inspire more players to embrace the elements and enjoy the game to the fullest. Happy golfing, rain or shine! ⛳☔ #RainyGolfChallenge #GolfEnthusiasts #MasteringTheElements\n","metadata":{"agentType":"specialist","functionStatus":"executed","processedAt":"2025-08-05T19:39:09.743Z","method":"processTask","originalParams":{"method":"process","prompt":"You write me a blog post about playing golf in the rain.","taskId":"796975b6-435b-4a51-a372-afcd981c1f6f","currentUser":{"id":"09f41d4d-1697-4141-a0de-3e258faae92b","email":"golfergeek@gmail.com","aud":"authenticated","role":"authenticated","appMetadata":{"provider":"email","providers":["email"]},"userMetadata":{"email_verified":true},"phone":"","emailConfirmedAt":"2025-05-18T18:46:51.491Z","confirmedAt":"2025-05-18T18:46:51.491Z","lastSignInAt":"2025-08-05T16:10:23.405Z","createdAt":"2025-05-18T18:46:51.474Z","updatedAt":"2025-08-05T18:56:33.394Z","identities":[{"identity_id":"7c4d7009-91f8-4e8b-b28d-7f8b52a17a0b","id":"09f41d4d-1697-4141-a0de-3e258faae92b","user_id":"09f41d4d-1697-4141-a0de-3e258faae92b","identity_data":{"email":"golfergeek@gmail.com","email_verified":false,"phone_verified":false,"sub":"09f41d4d-1697-4141-a0de-3e258faae92b"},"provider":"email","last_sign_in_at":"2025-05-18T18:46:51.48662Z","created_at":"2025-05-18T18:46:51.486679Z","updated_at":"2025-05-18T18:46:51.486679Z","email":"golfergeek@gmail.com"}]},"authToken":"eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IkxwM1hCMXIvL0ZEQzNUSjMiLCJ0eXAiOiJKV1QifQ..H2hrOWGYac3Kqm8i5n2880jCtQLK-rBBl7XcTGJGHdU","llmSelection":{"providerId":"7e157b23-07bb-47cd-9fe6-2c024d69ef6f","modelId":"494308ba-afb1-4bc8-983f-5acdec5920d4","cidafmOptions":{"activeStateModifiers":[],"responseModifiers":[],"executedCommands":[],"customOptions":{"customModifiers":[]}},"temperature":0.7},"conversationHistory":[{"role":"assistant","content":"Hello! I''m the Content. How can I help you today?","timestamp":"2025-08-05T19:37:27.111Z","metadata":{"isWelcome":true}},{"role":"user","content":"Write me a blog post about playing golf in the rain.","timestamp":"2025-08-05T19:37:34.460Z"},{"role":"user","content":"You write me a blog post about playing golf in the rain.","timestamp":"2025-08-05T19:38:46.253Z"}]},"agentName":"marketing-swarm","timestamp":"2025-08-05T19:38:47.307Z","taskId":"796975b6-435b-4a51-a372-afcd981c1f6f","processingType":"multi-agent-orchestration","processingTime":22180,"toolsUsed":["llm-service","langgraph","agent-coordination"],"responseType":"comprehensive-content-package","swarm_workflow":{"workflow_id":"swarm_1754422727308","sessionId":"unknown","steps_completed":["task_analysis","agent_selection","content_creation","evaluation","synthesis"],"start_time":"2025-08-05T19:38:47.308Z","analysis_step":"completed","task_complexity":"simple","content_types_needed":1,"agent_selection_step":"completed","selected_agent_count":4,"agent_names":["SEO Specialist","Brand Voice Analyst","Blog Post Writer","Social Media Specialist"],"content_creation_step":"completed","content_pieces_generated":2,"evaluation_step":"completed","evaluations_completed":2,"average_score":8,"synthesis_step":"completed","workflow_status":"completed","total_steps":5,"agents_utilized":4,"end_time":"2025-08-05T19:39:09.488Z"}}}', '{"taskId":"796975b6-435b-4a51-a372-afcd981c1f6f","userId":"09f41d4d-1697-4141-a0de-3e258faae92b","agentName":"Marketing Swarm","agentType":"specialist","toolsUsed":["llm-service","langgraph","agent-coordination"],"userEmail":"golfergeek@gmail.com","totalSteps":5,"processedAt":"2025-08-05T19:39:09.488Z","responseType":"comprehensive-content-package","processingTime":22180,"processingType":"multi-agent-orchestration","swarm_workflow":{"end_time":"2025-08-05T19:39:09.488Z","sessionId":"unknown","start_time":"2025-08-05T19:38:47.308Z","agent_names":["SEO Specialist","Brand Voice Analyst","Blog Post Writer","Social Media Specialist"],"total_steps":5,"workflow_id":"swarm_1754422727308","analysis_step":"completed","average_score":8,"synthesis_step":"completed","agents_utilized":4,"evaluation_step":"completed","steps_completed":["task_analysis","agent_selection","content_creation","evaluation","synthesis"],"task_complexity":"simple","workflow_status":"completed","agent_selection_step":"completed","content_types_needed":1,"selected_agent_count":4,"content_creation_step":"completed","evaluations_completed":2,"content_pieces_generated":2},"workflowStepsCompleted":["Analyzing marketing task","Selecting agent team","Coordinating content creation","Evaluating and optimizing","Synthesizing final content","Task execution completed"]}'::jsonb, 'completed', 100, 'Task created, waiting for execution...', '{}'::jsonb, '{"createdAt":"2025-08-05T19:38:46.898Z","originalLLMSelection":{"modelId":"494308ba-afb1-4bc8-983f-5acdec5920d4","providerId":"7e157b23-07bb-47cd-9fe6-2c024d69ef6f","temperature":0.7,"cidafmOptions":{"customOptions":{"customModifiers":[]},"executedCommands":[],"responseModifiers":[],"activeStateModifiers":[]}}}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-08-05T19:39:09.488+00:00', 300, '{}'::jsonb, '2025-08-05T19:38:47.07592+00:00', '2025-08-05T19:39:09.951222+00:00', 'text', '{}'::jsonb),
  ('ab9b7b22-b79a-4d39-8ad1-ab1d0fcf1474', '52d6b373-7f83-4eac-b9ff-e42b7f168f29', 'db94682e-5184-496f-93fd-dc739aa0f9e7', 'executeTask', 'Write requirements for a simple todo list application. Include user stories, functional requirements, and technical specifications.', '{}'::jsonb, '{"success":true,"response":"# Product Requirements Document (PRD) for Simple Todo List Application\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\nThe simple todo list application aims to provide users with a user-friendly interface for creating, managing, and organizing their tasks efficiently. This application will enhance user productivity by allowing them to prioritize tasks, mark tasks as completed, and securely store task details. The key features include task creation, deletion, completion, prioritization, user authentication, data encryption, and a seamless frontend UI.\n\n## 2. Product Overview\n**Goals:**  \n- Provide users with a simple and intuitive todo list application.\n- Improve task management and organization for users.\n- Ensure data security and privacy through encryption techniques.\n\n**Objectives:**  \n- Develop a frontend UI for task management.\n- Implement backend server logic for task operations.\n- Integrate user authentication and data encryption for security.\n- Enable users to create, delete, complete, and prioritize tasks.\n\n**Success Metrics:**  \n- User engagement metrics (daily active users, session duration).\n- Task completion rate.\n- User satisfaction through feedback and ratings.\n\n## 3. User Personas & Use Cases\n**User Persona:**  \n- **Name:** Emily\n- **Background:** Working professional juggling multiple tasks.\n- **Needs:** Easy task creation, clear task prioritization, secure task storage.\n\n**Use Cases:**  \n1. Emily wants to create a new task with a due date.\n2. Emily needs to mark a task as completed.\n3. Emily wishes to prioritize tasks based on urgency.\n4. Emily wants to delete a task that is no longer relevant.\n\n## 4. Functional Requirements\n1. Task Creation:\n   - Users can create a new task with a title, description, and due date.\n2. Task Deletion:\n   - Users can delete a task from the task list.\n3. Task Completion:\n   - Users can mark a task as completed.\n4. Task Prioritization:\n   - Users can prioritize tasks by setting their urgency level.\n5. Frontend UI:\n   - Develop a responsive and user-friendly interface for task management.\n6. Backend Server:\n   - Implement server-side logic for handling task operations.\n7. Database for Task Storage:\n   - Set up a database to store task details securely.\n8. Task List Display:\n   - Display all tasks in a clear and organized manner.\n9. Task Creation Form:\n   - Provide a form for users to input task details.\n10. Task Detail View:\n    - Allow users to view detailed information about a specific task.\n11. User Authentication:\n    - Implement a secure login system for user authentication.\n12. Data Encryption for Task Details:\n    - Encrypt task details to ensure data privacy and security.\n\n## 5. User Stories\n1. As a user, I want to be able to create a new task with a title and due date.\n   - **Acceptance Criteria:** Task must have a title and a valid due date.\n   - **Workflow:** User clicks on \"Add Task\", fills in task details, and saves the task.\n2. As a user, I want to mark a task as completed.\n   - **Acceptance Criteria:** Completed tasks should be visually distinguishable.\n   - **Workflow:** User selects a task and marks it as completed.\n3. As a user, I want to prioritize tasks based on urgency.\n   - **Acceptance Criteria:** Tasks should be sortable by priority level.\n   - **Workflow:** User rearranges tasks based on priority.\n\n## 6. Non-Functional Requirements\n- **Performance:** Ensure fast loading times for task lists.\n- **Security:** Implement secure user authentication and data encryption.\n- **Scalability:** Design the application to handle a growing number of users and tasks.\n\n## 7. Technical Considerations\n- **Frontend:** Use React.js for building the frontend UI.\n- **Backend:** Employ Node.js for server-side logic.\n- **Database:** Utilize MongoDB for storing task details.\n- **Security:** Implement JWT for user authentication and AES encryption for data security.\n\n## 8. Implementation Timeline\n1. **Week 1-2:** Design frontend UI and task creation form.\n2. **Week 3-4:** Develop backend server logic and database integration.\n3. **Week 5:** Implement user authentication and data encryption.\n4. **Week 6:** Conduct testing and bug fixing.\n5. **Week 7:** Deploy the application for user testing.\n\n## 9. Success Metrics\n- **KPIs:** Daily active users, task completion rate, user feedback ratings.\n- **Measurement Criteria:** Increase in user engagement, positive user reviews, reduced task management time.\n\n## 10. Risk Assessment\n**Challenges:**\n- Integration issues between frontend and backend components.\n- Ensuring data security and encryption implementation.\n- User acceptance and adoption of the application.\n\n**Mitigation Strategies:**\n- Conduct thorough testing and debugging during development.\n- Implement security best practices and conduct security audits.\n- Gather user feedback early on and iterate based on user preferences.\n\nThis Product Requirements Document outlines the key features, requirements, and considerations for the development of the simple todo list application. It serves as a roadmap for the successful implementation and launch of the product.","metadata":{"agentType":"engineering","executionType":"python_script","scriptPath":"/Users/golfergeek/projects/golfergeek/orchestrator-ai/apps/api/src/agents/actual/engineering/requirements_writer/agent-function.py","processedAt":"2025-08-06T11:36:23.673Z","method":"processTask","originalParams":{"method":"executeTask","prompt":"Write requirements for a simple todo list application. Include user stories, functional requirements, and technical specifications.","taskId":"ab9b7b22-b79a-4d39-8ad1-ab1d0fcf1